. *-------------------------------------------------------------------------
. * 9. Bug 4 closure -- explicit cluster() at the SAME grouping as the
. *    default (panel id), away from the singular-S2 regime of Case 5.
. *
. * Case 5 (cluster(region_id), 20 clusters vs 90 instruments) sits inside the
. * singular-moment-matrix regime, so it cannot cleanly isolate the qc-factor
. * fix (GMMEngine._cluster_qc_factor) from the separate, unresolved
. * generalized-inverse divergence documented there. This case avoids that
. * confound entirely: cluster(country_id) has 200 clusters against ~90
. * instruments (same as the no-cluster() case below), so S2 is always full
. * rank. The only thing that should differ between 9a and 9b is whether the
. * small-sample N_clusters/(N_clusters-1) factor is applied:
. *   - 9a (no cluster(), default clustering by panel id): xtabond2.mata:564's
. *     rows(clusts)==0 branch applies N_clusters/(N_clusters-1) = 200/199.
. *   - 9b (explicit cluster(country_id), identical grouping): Mata's
. *     rows(clusts)!=0 branch drops that factor entirely.
. * Beta should be IDENTICAL between 9a/9b (same grouping, same moment
. * matrix); SE should differ by exactly sqrt(199/200) =~ 0.997497 (9b smaller
. * than 9a). This is precisely the comparison the Methodological Note (Bug 4)
. * flags as still needed for an independent, non-confounded Stata check.
. *
. * Python (from compute_python_reference.py, case 9a/9b):
. *   9a see PYTHON_9A_PLACEHOLDER -- fill in after running
. *     compute_python_reference.py, or just diff python_reference_output.txt.
. *   9b see PYTHON_9B_PLACEHOLDER
. * Expected: 9a and 9b betas identical; 9a/9b SE ratio = sqrt(199/200) exactly.
. *-------------------------------------------------------------------------
. di as txt _n "=== 9a. No cluster() (default = panel id), twostep robust small ==="

